    "note": "Kyiv Hydroelectric Power Plant’s prewar low spillway and powerhouse, blue reservoir-side rail, two gantries, control tower, quay walls, navigation lock and road bridge. The main exterior and reservoir-side rail follow dated 2018 and 2020 photographs. The lock follows the photograph taken June 12, 2021, which is the represented date. The viewing interval ends before the full-scale invasion. It is a conservative display scope and does not identify a date when the plant changed. The signed vertical origin is 98.004144 m. The crest road is approximately 107.2 m. The design review uses 103 m headwater, 91.5 m tailwater and 96.1 m illustrative chamber stage. Historical placement requires an explicit viewingDate within the recorded appearance interval; excluded from the default current world."
